OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,4,F
OL,5, British Rail has accepted full
OL,6, responsibility for the train crash in
OL,7, Glasgow in which two people, including
OL,8, a driver, were killed and 49 injured.
OL,10,FThe surviving driver and four
OL,11,Fpassengers are seriously injured.
OL,13,FThe 1220 Milngavie to Springburn and
OL,14,Fthe 1239 Springburn to Milngavie
OL,15,Fcollided head-on in a cutting outside
OL,16,FBellgrove station, just before 1300.
OL,18,FThe Queen has said in a message to the
OL,19,FGovernment she was "greatly distressed
OL,20,Fto hear of yet another rail accident
OL,21,Finvolving injury and loss of life".
OL,23,T]CFrom 06-03-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,185,190,120,250,0,100
PN,18403
SC,0003
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F184A1772832104
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G3/10
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, One of the trains involved in the crash
OL,6, in Glasgow in which two people died is
OL,7, said to have been running late.
OL,9,FOne report says the late train, heading
OL,10,Ffor Milngavie, should have been clear
OL,11,Fof the section of single line track
OL,12,Fwhere the trains crashed head-on.
OL,14,FA signalman tried to avert the accident
OL,15,Fby exploding two trackside detonators
OL,16,Fwhen he realised a crash was imminent.
OL,18,FBritish Rail has launched a full
OL,19,Finquiry into the cause of the crash.
OL,23,T]CFrom 06-03-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,185,190,120,250,0,100
PN,18404
SC,0004
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F184A1772832104
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G4/10
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Rescuers faced problems reaching the
OL,6, scene of the train crash in Glasgow
OL,7, because of the steep sides of the
OL,8, cutting where the accident happened.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FEmergency teams for four hours to free
OL,11,Ftwo people, including the surviving
OL,12,Fdriver.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FReports said the leading coach of one
OL,15,Ftrain rode up over the front of the
OL,16,Fsecond and some coaches were derailed.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThere were about 70 people on the
OL,19,Ftrains, which were travelling in
OL,20,Fopposite directions on the same stretch
OL,21,Fof track at about 30 miles an hour.
OL,23,T]CFrom 06-03-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,185,190,120,250,0,100
PN,18405
SC,0005
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F184A1772832104
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/10
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, British Rail chairman Sir Robert Reid
OL,6, has denied claims that BR management
OL,7, has admitted putting passengers'
OL,8, comfort and convenience before safety.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FIn a letter to Labour's transport
OL,11,Fspokesman Mr John Prescott, he said
OL,12,Fsafety was always BR's first priority.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FMr Prescott attacked BR after the
OL,15,Fcompany's counsel at the Clapham rail
OL,16,Finquiry said it could be seen with
OL,17,Fhindsight that plans for signal
OL,18,Fmodernisation had compromised safety.
OL,20,FMr Prescott said Sir Robert's letter
OL,21,Fwas an admission of guilt.
OL,23,T]CFrom 06-03-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,185,190,120,250,0,100
PN,18406
SC,0006
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F184A1772832104
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/10
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Transport Secritary Mr Paul Channon has
OL,6, told MPs there will be an independent
OL,7, public inquiry into Saturday's crash at
OL,8, Purley in which five people died.
OL,10,FMr Channon said he had appointed the
OL,11,Fdeputy chief inspecting officer of the
OL,12,FRailway Inspectorate, Mr Alan Cooksey,
OL,13,Fas head of the inquiry.
OL,15,FHe denied Opposition claims that the
OL,16,FGovernment had under-invested in
OL,17,FBritish Rail.
OL,19,FMr Channon told MPs he had just heard
OL,20,Freports of the rail crash in Glasgow
OL,21,Fbefore making his statement.
OL,23,T]CFrom 06-03-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,185,190,120,250,0,100
PN,18407
SC,0007
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F184A1772832104
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G7/10
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, British Rail has said evidence points
OL,6, to human error as the cause of
OL,7, Saturday's crash at Purley in Surrey
OL,8, in which five people died.
OL,10,FA spokesman emphasised this was only
OL,11,Fa preliminary conclusion.
OL,13,FHe said evidence collected from staff
OL,14,Fsupported the earlier reports of an
OL,15,Ferror by one of the drivers. One had
OL,16,Fsaid he drove through a red signal.
OL,18,FA BR statement said no signalling,
OL,19,Ftrack or braking faults had been found.
OL,20,FBritish Rail's internal inquiry into
OL,21,Fthe accident is continuing.
OL,23,T]CFrom 06-03-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
