OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F184A1772832104
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G8/10
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, China has called for an international
OL,6, fund to be set up to help protect the
OL,7, world's ozone layer.
OL,9,FThe Chinese delegate told the London
OL,10,FSaving the Ozone Layer conference that
OL,11,Fthe fund would help developing
OL,12,Fcountries to switch from harmful CFCs,
OL,13,Fchlorofluorocarbons, to substitutes.
OL,15,FEarlier, developing countries had
OL,16,Fexpressed concern that a ban on CFCs
OL,17,Fcould threaten their industrialisation.
OL,19,FSoviet officials have again stressed
OL,20,Fthe need to move ahead cautiously until
OL,21,Fthere is more evidence of ozone damage.
OL,23,T]CFrom 06-03-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
